'''Kevin Ray Turner''' (born February 5, 1958) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[linebacker]] in the [[National Football League]] (NFL) for the [[New York Giants]], [[Washington Redskins]], [[Seattle Seahawks]], and [[Cleveland Browns]]. He played [[college football]] for the [[Pacific Tigers football|Pacific Tigers]].

